  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through Thursday)\nIssued at 1206 AM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nAt least isolated convection is expected to develop by late Friday\nafternoon or more likely early Friday evening along the advancing\ncold front. Strong downburst winds will be possible with the\nstronger storms. These storms will likely exit the area or \ndissipate by near or shortly after midnight as the front clears \nthe area. \n\nMuch cooler and less humid conditions will then prevail over the\nweekend before a warming trend begins early next week.\nTemperatures will return to above normal levels by the latter half\nof next week, but dew points should remain lower than they have\nbeen this week.",
